rams" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050587 #edb/ref 1033 794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050587 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5608f963-4aa6-51e0-b27f-7406f85dcd4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157084 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7153" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157084 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the sets $X = \\{2, 5, 7, 8\\},$ $Y = \\{1, 3, 5\\},$ and $Z = \\{2, 4, 6, 8\\},$ find $X \\cup Y,$ $Y \\cup Z,$ and $Z \\cup X.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157084 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99f04ab6-00a0-5ccc-a328-49a85547c4c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157084 #edb/ref 1074 "The union $X \\cup Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X\\cup Y & =\\{2,5,7,8\\}\\cup \\{1,3,5\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,2,3,5,7,8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe union $Y \\cup Z$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $Y$ or $Z,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y\\cup Z & =\\{1,3,5\\}\\cup \\{2,4,6,8\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,2,3,4,5,6,8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe union $Z \\cup X$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $Z$ or $X,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z\\cup X & =\\{2,4,6,8\\}\\cup \\{2,5,7,8\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,4,5,6,7,8\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157085 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7154" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157085 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ and $B$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ and the set of all multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0,$ respectively. What is $A \\cup B?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157085 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6a3a434d-5fe4-53cd-ba34-4d10db5c85fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157085 #edb/ref 1074 "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA = \\{ 4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32, 36 \\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $6$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB = \\{ 6,12,18,24,30,36,\\ldots \\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A \\cup B$ is the *union* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in either $A$ or $B,$ or both.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cup B & =\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,36,…\\}\\cup \\{6,12,18,24,30,36,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{4,6,8,12,16,18,20,24,28,30,32,36,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157095 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7171" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157095 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/dc/dcddc9ee6fe49965ea4f261fcb43c6f7ccd14193910e864b950745ef513e67a6.png)\n\nThe sets $X = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 \\}$ and $Y = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}$ are shown in the Venn diagram above. Find $X\\cup Y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157095 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3de58ae0-eb3a-5faf-a404-0347d64d4979" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157095 #edb/ref 1074 "The union $X \\cup Y$ consists of all the elements that are in $X$ or $Y,$ or both. To represent $X \\cup Y,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained within either $X$ or $Y,$ or both.\n\n![](images/c9/c94cfc38872dfe0673e112e09feec7781ab4f247f08932d1d8ecd167b4a99d32.png)\n\nThe elements $1,2,3,4,5,8$ are in either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. Therefore, the union of $X$ and $Y$ is\n\n$$\nX \\cup Y = \\{ 1,2,3,4,5,8 \\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157280 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186157566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157280 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186157567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157280 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157280 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157280 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186554566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157280 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186554627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157280 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Union of Sets Without a Venn Diagram" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157280 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186157084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157280 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "65d40bd9-4d35-5e07-a767-8b2ae6ba559a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157281 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186157765 #edb/ref 17592186045417