483504921bb3fad4cbeedba4ca812bb20ef7ba96f637b7.svg) is the set of all elements belonging to either ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) or ![](images/65/65ada9c919fe5c4bee19fb4cafff28ed46a36bf6fc90b4cecf70e0fa02386ce0.svg) or both.\n\nFor example, consider the sets ![](images/32/3228232fb4c16493d5268b308ede8727a84c20297d9b216a74db7b537011c704.svg) and ![](images/4d/4d576c7a3682975f73724c0fbddaf962449049968b852a28434102128ffa8a96.svg) We can represent these sets using a Venn diagram, as follows:\n\n![](images/83/8351db4817ac8b0d2991fe8ef09ee1f2583c84cb772114ef0614a0ef96c96389.png)\n\nThe union ![](images/58/58a13b2e88b95997772105b179139f2bb67105050519a451c17b838337cb4632.svg) consists of all the elements that are in ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) or ![](images/65/65ada9c919fe5c4bee19fb4cafff28ed46a36bf6fc90b4cecf70e0fa02386ce0.svg) or both. To represent ![](images/18/18271071563c5a2bcf483504921bb3fad4cbeedba4ca812bb20ef7ba96f637b7.svg) we will shade in all the area that is contained within either ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) or ![](images/65/65ada9c919fe5c4bee19fb4cafff28ed46a36bf6fc90b4cecf70e0fa02386ce0.svg) or both.\n\n![](images/e9/e912fe53d530ac47245c916bd16f1758df487ded32da88abfab253ed1ee0cc63.png)\n\nThe elements ![](images/0e/0e9479f799610ac47cadcc6890bb35f5336c08c9e2827384fd299138b7e4c558.svg) are in either ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) or ![](images/65/65ada9c919fe5c4bee19fb4cafff28ed46a36bf6fc90b4cecf70e0fa02386ce0.svg) or both. Therefore, the union of ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) and ![](images/75/7533ad047439b7d799dd7afee5d6a7bc9f4404fbadb8c3f27ef6d3952119ff6b.svg) is\n\n![](images/dc/dc7e001d55359f56770a3cdd382a7318d77cbb12b260141399192d14953b4146.svg)\n\nNotice that ![](images/a7/a77a353782459b753313d80235712695d65dc4a44d8d357aa41add6729f81d8f.svg) belongs to both ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) and ![](images/65/65ada9c919fe5c4bee19fb4cafff28ed46a36bf6fc90b4cecf70e0fa02386ce0.svg) but we list it only once in ![](images/bb/bbb285be6a3e138649aa4a514c34823a6b39d094dca3427eb34eb4a326854fcf.svg) In a set, each distinct element is written only once." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158472 #edb/ref 1065 4331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158472 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7d7d339f-bbdd-5e0c-9913-c3e6cdc13958" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158472 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158478 #edb/ref 1064 "Although Venn diagrams can be useful to visualize unions, we do not have to draw a Venn diagram every time we wish to compute a union.\n\nFor example, let's again consider the sets $A = \\{ a,b,c \\}$ and $B = \\{ b, d, e \\}.$ This time, we will compute the union $A \\cup B$ without using a Venn diagram. We just need to find all the elements that are in either $A$ or $B,$ or both.\n\nSo, we will start with the elements of $A,$ and then go through the elements of $B$ to look for any elements that we do not already have. Remember that we are looking for elements that we do *not* already have in $A.$\n\n- For the element $b \\in B,$ we have $b \\in A. \\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- For the element $d \\in B,$ we have $d \\not \\in A. \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- For the element $e \\in B,$ we have $e \\not \\in A. \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nSo, to get the union, we need to take the elements of $A$ and also include $d$ and $e.$\n\nTherefore, the union of $A$ and $B$ is\n\n$$\nA \\cup B = \\{ a,b,c,d,e \\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158478 #edb/ref 1065 4338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158478 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "387bbd7c-3300-588c-9e61-54dda9490e81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158478 #edb/ref 1067 "Unions Without Venn Diagrams" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233058 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233058 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102051" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233058 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233058 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1f/1f3d0b514bc4ec701b6ac755b82cec7246a7a819400108e1733759eb0a2fec86.png)\n\nGiven the sets $A=\\{o,p,q,r\\}$ and $B=\\{q,r,v,w\\},$ find $A\\cup B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233058 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2a78df4-f852-500a-b23e-2d5ff58187c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233058 #edb/ref 1074 "The union $A\\cup B$ consists of all the elements that are in either $A$ or $B,$ or both. To represent $A\\cup B,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in either $A$ or $B,$ or both.\n\n![](images/79/7984b0cb81df816388aa0d5cbf860fc4bdad9f7e871e8671d4616ded02bcaf5b.png)\n\nThe elements $o,p,q,r,v,w$ are in either $A$ or $B$, or both. Therefore, the union of $A$ and $B$ is\n\n$$\nA\\cup B=\\{o,p,q,r,v,w\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234433 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234433 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81562" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234433 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234433 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ and $B$ be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0$ and the set of all multiples of $5$ greater than $0,$ respectively. What is $A\\cup B?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234433 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "26c3bb06-29af-54da-a6db-d70352bbb70a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186234433 #edb/ref 1074 "The multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA=\\{4,8,12,16,20,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB=\\{5,10,15,20,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $A\\cup B$ is the *union* of $A$ and $B,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in either $A$ or $B,$ or both. In other words, $A\\cup B$ denotes the set of natural numbers that are either multiple of $4$ or multiple of $5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cup B & =\\{4,8,12,16,20,…\\}\\cup \\{5,10,15,20,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{4,5,8,10,12,15,16,20,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553895 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{7,25,50\\}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553895 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553895 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0cbb00e8-fa3a-5a23-a8f1-0bae0667c2ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553903 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{3,7,19,21\\}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553903 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553903 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10b45b2c-b1e5-51df-9233-681766e27744" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553917 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{o,p,q,r,v,w,x\\}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553917 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553917 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1959e253-4fde-51cc-90d9-1cc12992f1d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553927 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{105,108,119,122,135\\}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553927 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553927 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21ec46e2-7cea-500e-85fb-33a7017558ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553931 #edb/ref 1080 "∅" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553931 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553931 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23a4ac02-1db6-583f-82e6-b5db013364aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553954 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{7,25\\}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553954 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553954 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f08521a-3060-562d-954a-c40b0f5aa7e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553955 #edb/ref 1080 "\\{1,3,4,8,9,12,16,20,24,27,…\\}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553955 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553955 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f3ce74f-3cd9-5ddc-870f-ba877c7553c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186553988 #e