" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554495 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554495 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ac450825-0a43-5655-9b1b-af418583e6b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554566 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554566 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102074" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554566 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554566 #edb/ref 1071 "If $X=\\{105,118,119,123,135\\}$ and $Y=\\{108,119,122,123\\}$, then $X\\cup Y=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554566 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ece29a0-cc0f-5be6-9001-b8cc96566290" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554566 #edb/ref 1074 "The set $X\\cup Y$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X\\cup Y & =\\{105,118,119,123,135\\}\\cup \\{108,119,122,123\\} \\\\  & =\\{105,108,118,119,122,123,135\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554617 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554617 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554617 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554617 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e2/e27737b6aac8caa70549393b78c11ea3d6cc97cb54ec51b557744dfc456359d0.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S=\\{7,9\\}$ and $T=\\{10,25,50\\},$ find $S\\cup T.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554617 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b53fe7a0-ceb1-5bb0-aa72-c767bfb8907a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554617 #edb/ref 1074 "The union $S\\cup T$ consists of all the elements that are in either $S$ or $T,$ or both. To represent $S\\cup T,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in either $S$ or $T,$ or both.\n\n![](images/34/34587d9fc3201b9251d233a813d96ed355b8285e64dd1b7d71c72f91c8ee5efb.png)\n\nThe elements $7,9,10,25,50$ are in either $S$ or $T.$ Therefore, the union of $S$ and $T$ is\n\n$$\nS\\cup T=\\{7,9,10,25,50\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554618 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554618 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102147" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554618 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554618 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be the set of all non-negative integer powers of $3$ and the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0,$ respectively. What is $X\\cup Y?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554618 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b7be71bb-2a94-5959-b6e1-bd279930afab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554618 #edb/ref 1074 "The non-negative integer powers of $3$ are\n\n$$\nX=\\{1,3,9,27,…\\}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nY=\\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, $X\\cup Y$ is the *union* of $X$ and $Y,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in either $X$ or $Y,$ or both. In other words, $X\\cup Y$ denotes the set of natural numbers that are either powers of $3$ or multiples of  $4.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X\\cup Y & =\\{1,3,9,27,…\\}\\cup \\{4,8,12,16,20,24,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{1,3,4,8,9,12,16,20,24,27,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554627 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554627 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36187" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554627 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554627 #edb/ref 1071 "If $A=\\{3,5,7,19,21,115\\}$ and $B=\\{2,3,4,7,16,19,21,22\\},$ then $A\\cup B=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554627 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3ebe755-cc28-56a9-a6f9-b3ea716cdfc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554627 #edb/ref 1074 "The set $A\\cup B$ is the set of all elements belonging to either $A$ or $B,$ or both. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cup B & =\\{3,5,7,19,21,115\\}\\cup \\{2,3,4,7,16,19,21,22\\} \\\\  & =\\{2,3,4,5,7,16,19,21,22,115\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
